From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Size video for the largest screen that is on

Media3 (ExoPlayer) caps video at the physical size of the default display's mode, through
Util.getCurrentDisplayModeSize(). The default display is the cover (port 132), 748x720, so
players offered at most 480p in DeX and while mirroring, even on a 1080p monitor. FPT Play
and Just Player both showed it.

For app processes, Display.getMode() on the cover now reports the physical size of the
largest display that is on, such as the DeX desktop or the inner panel. The mode keeps the
cover's id, refresh rate, vsync rate, alternative refresh rates, and HDR types. With only the
cover on, nothing changes, so video on the cover stays sized for the cover. System processes
see the real mode. The lookup asks DisplayManager for the other displays, so it runs after
Display.mLock is released.

Known limits:
- An app drawn on the cover sees the larger size too while another display is on.
- The reported mode no longer matches an entry of getSupportedModes() by size.
- The size changes without a display-changed event for the cover; players read it when they
  start, so a player opened before DeX keeps its old cap until it restarts.

